Need I state the obvious?  Pacifist conduct is hard. But this game
was a great learning experience.

This was about my 50th pacifist attempt.  The second one to make it past
the Valley of the Dead.

The opening was non-descript.  I visited minetown first; bought 9 protection,
found a polytrap and had a yellow dragon and elvenking as pets.  The
elvenking died on the Medusa level fighting a Titan summoning storm.  The
yellow dragon was eaten by a trapper in Hell.

The middle game: I found 5 magic markers, a magic lamp, and a wand
of wishing somewhere between Dlvls 10-18.  Eventually, I had -40 AC,
~120 HP, 6 XP.  I made a base at a neutral altar on Dlvl:14.

I found some graveyards and the VotD brought me to 13 XP.

Out of four figurines of an Archon I had wished for only two were tame.  The
first tame Archon I had became peaceful when I lost him to a level-teleport
trap on dungeon level 48.  He wound up on dungeon level <5. I did not find
him fast enough.  The second tame Archon had +6 Demonbane, +5 Shield of
Reflection, +5 leather gloves, +4 leather hat, and +0 unicorn horn. I forgot
to give him boots.  More importantly I wished for two potions of gain level
and my Archon and I split the two.  I became XP:14 and he XP:29.  This
enabled him to defeat Orcus, but my careless use of wishes and the current
level of my Archon would lead to my downfall as a pacifist.

11 wishes:
 WoW (0:1) : ?oCharging, SDSM, Orb of Fate, Magicbane, figurine (non-tame)
 magic lamp: figurine (first tame archon)
 WoW (0:1) : figurine (non-tame), figurine (second tame archon), 2!oGL,
             bag of holding, magic marker.

Careless wishes: SDSM (I had an amulet of reflection), Orb of Fate,
Magicbane, magic marker (I already had enough of these) and bag of holding.
I wished for the artifacts to make sure I would survive and not have to
worry much about curses.  In retrospect (wizard mode) this was overkill
[ eventually I genocided 20 monsters: ctwLh ]. The other wishes were
just out of impatience.

When I met the wizard, I had zapped a wand of digging at his island and he
immediately drank a potion of gain level (XP:31).  Then he stole the Staff.
My Archon was only level 29 and I had burned all my wishes at that point.
I teleported back to level 14 where my stuff was; hoping to find a potion
of gain level or at least a potion of levitation. I had none. So I mixed
and drank 8 blessed potions of extra healing (smoky) and did not summon
a single djinni.

I decided to fully explore the mines in hopes of finding new potions and in
my haste ran into and killed a lichen (turn 65k).  I did not find a single
wand of polymorph in the game either.  I had an aversion to searching through
Hell for extra objects because of fear of losing my pet Archon.  I did not
have the spell of charm monster. Plus I was nowhere near the XP to tame an
Archon.  Even if I had not run into that lichen I would probably have
voluntarily ditched the pacifist conduct.

I'm wondering, even though I left the wizard on dungeon level 14; would he
have eventually teleported to the current dungeon level I was on?  He still
had the Book of the Dead, and had stolen my quest artifact, the candelabrum,
and the bell.

So I ascended my first healer (353595 points, 192/304 HPs) [only Ranger
and Archeologist left].  Next time I'll remember to leave spare wishes--
but I always say that ;).

